  "authored_scope": "Random scenes vary grid size (12-24 by default; 8-30 accepted, non-square allowed), centre position, tip distances 1-3, shape lengths 2-8 and lateral extents. Shape segments can be solid, axis-holed, combs closed by solid rows, or one-sided. Colours and the winning direction vary, and the background is configurable (default 8). Every fixture is 16x16 with background 8, so other sizes, other backgrounds and tip distance 3 are synthetic extensions. Deliberately not sampled: a winner whose farthest cell lies off the centre axis (the fixtures do not decide the stamp location there); disconnected or interleaved shapes; ties for largest; a non-unique random centre.",
  "authored_constraints": [
    "Each shape is a single colour forming one 8-connected component, strictly on its own side of the centre.",
    "Shapes are mutually 8-separated and the four colours are distinct and differ from the background.",
    "Vertical and horizontal tips are never both at distance 1, so tips do not touch diagonally.",
    "The largest shape is strictly largest by cell count.",
    "The background is a strict majority of the grid.",
    "The random centre is the unique minimum-ray-total four-colour centre. Explicit scenes may rely on the row-major-first tie-break, matching the reference.",
    "The winner's farthest cell on the axis equals its overall depth, so the stamp lies wholly beyond the shape.",
    "The stamp cells are in-grid background and not 8-adjacent to any loser.",
    "About 35% of scenes contain a decoy loser that is deeper, has a larger bounding box, or has a nearer tip than the winner."
  ],
